+    // not evidence of a fake. A stitched core fake scores high on fake and LOW on both real classes,
+    // so it keeps its full penalty. Crediting with the displaced score alone measured EQUIVALENT
+    // within noise on every axis, so this choice is not load-bearing.
+    //
+    // MEASURED TRADE, and it does not have a free lunch in it (jets tune + 120 events of PU200 RelVal
+    // event_1000, P2's validated claim replay): the credit removes the differential tax monotonically
+    // -- displaced-true chains pay 3.5x the prompt tax at k = 0 and 1.2x at k = 5 -- but the jet-core
+    // gain falls with it: ~86% of the uncredited gain at k = 0.25, ~60% at k = 1.5, ~27% at k = 5,
+    // while the displaced cells only come fully clean at the k = 5 end. NO value of k keeps 80% of
+    // the jet gain and clears the displaced cells; the full trade curve, including the two rejected
+    // scale-free "ratio" forms (which keep the jet gain and do NOT relieve the tax), is in
+    // standalone/FINDINGS_JETROUND.md.
+    float orderT3DispCredit = 0.f;
